-- title:
--   Coefficient ring for the completed stalk at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L \subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K_2$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K_2$, let $j_2 \in K_2$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\mathfrak{X}_2 = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K_2\,j_2$, the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebras of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$, respectively over $A[j_2^{-1}]$. Let $z_2$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}_2$ such that the germ at $z_2$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism $\mathfrak{X}_2 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O} = \mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X}_2, z_2}$, let $y_2$ be a point of the finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_2\,j_2)$ mapping to $z_2$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y_2$, the value $\varphi(j_2)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Finally let $\mathfrak{y}_2$ be an ideal of the finite chart algebra equal to the prime of $y_2$. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W_2$, a ring homomorphism $\tau_2 : A \to W_2$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $\tau_2(\varpi)$, and a ring homomorphism $\sigma_2$ from $W_2$ to the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}$ of $\mathcal{O}$, such that $\sigma_2(\tau_2(a))$ is, for every $a \in A$, the image in $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}$ of the germ at $z_2$ of $a$ pulled back along the structure morphism, and such that every $f \in \mathcal{O}$ satisfies $f - \sigma_2(o) \in \mathfrak{m}\widehat{\mathcal{O}}$ in $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}$ for some $o \in W_2$.
--
--   This is the coefficient-ring half of a Cohen-type structure statement for the completed local ring of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ at a point of the special fibre with supersingular $j$-invariant: $W_2$ plays the role of the unramified extension of the completion of $A$ with residue field that of the point, $\tau_2$ records the base, and $\sigma_2$ is a lift which is surjective onto the residue field. It is used in the analysis of the completed stalk as a crossing of two branches, which identifies it with a quotient of a two-variable power series ring over $W_2$.
